# EVERY NOTE A DOCUMENT OWES ON ITS OWN FACE. One row per (filing, note) that must be VISIBLE,
# not merely present.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE RULE THAT DECIDES MEMBERSHIP: A NOTE IS OWED WHEREVER THE NOTATION'S OWN DEFAULT
#    READING IS WRONG. Not everything true about a filing belongs on its face. These four do,
#    because without each one a reader reaches a specific false conclusion from a correct drawing:
#      scope       a pool with three lanes reads as *this is the system*. It is a PROJECTION, and
#                  14 of 15 filings here decline to claim otherwise.
#      search      an absent dependence line reads as INDEPENDENCE. 12 of 15 state no coupling and
#                  the four typed answers are the only thing separating *nobody looked* from
#                  *somebody looked and found none*.
#      dependence  a dotted arrow between two lanes reads as FLOW. A coupling is a dependence and
#                  is NEVER evidence for a fusion, which the schema says in capitals.
#      cover       a dashed box around nodes reads as a CONTAINER. A group is a cover: an
#                  operation may be in several and is in exactly one lane.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND `documentation` PUTS ALL OF THEM IN THE ARTIFACT AND ON NO PAGE. It is an ANNOTATION
#   admitted on any base element and INVISIBLE in every rendering. `textAnnotation` is the only
#   element in BPMN that puts words on the canvas, and withholding it on the reason
#   *documentation is spent instead* is true, and about the wrong
#   property. Two readers need two carriers: a tool reads the documentation where it is attached,
#   a person reads the note where it is drawn.
#
# ⭐⭐ FLOATING, WITH NO `association`. An artifact may stand alone, and attaching these would
#    spend `association` a second way, which is exactly the collision that ruled it out for `F`:
#    the two consolidation filings already carry coupling lines and would carry note lines beside
#    them, and a reader could not tell which dotted line was which.
#
# ⚠️ CONDITIONAL ON PAGE THREE AND FOUR. A document with no coupling owes no note about arrows,
#   and one with no cover owes none about dashed boxes. A legend for a glyph that is not there is
#   noise, and noise is how a legend stops being read.
#
# ⭐⭐ AND EACH NOTE NAMES THE RELATION IT STATES, FOR THE REASON THE `--` LINE EXISTS. These
#    four are the only sentences in this pipeline a person reads off a PICTURE, so they are the
#    ones furthest from the model and the ones with no other route back to it.
#    `diagrams/annotated.sqlc` carries the same column for the sentences a tool reads.
-- the notes a correct reading requires; BPMN 2.0 tTextAnnotation, drawn and unattached.
SELECT s.filing, 'scope' AS note, 'diagrams/scopes.sqlc' AS states
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/scopes.sqlc) ) s
UNION ALL
SELECT s.filing, 'search', 'diagrams/searches.sqlc'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/searches.sqlc) ) s
UNION ALL
SELECT DISTINCT d.filing, 'dependence', 'diagrams/dependences.sqlc'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/dependences.sqlc) ) d
UNION ALL
SELECT DISTINCT c.filing, 'cover', 'diagrams/categories.sqlc'
FROM ( :compose(diagrams/categories.sqlc) ) c
